    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d66">

                <pb facs="0232" n="100" xml:id="pg100"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 E. W./6–1545: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 66 <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Political Adviser for German Affairs</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Murphy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Director of
                        European Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Matthews</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d66-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-06-15T22:00:00+02:00">June 15, 1945—10
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3612. (For Matthews from Murphy. No other distribution.)</p>
                <p> General Eisenhower has telegraphed Deane<anchor n="2" xml:id="d66-f2"/> that he
                    is sending to Berlin on June 17 a group of officers and enlisted personnel to
                    hold preliminary conference with representatives of Marshal Zhukov for the
                    purpose of making necessary advance arrangements for the meeting in Berlin on
                    July 15. The arrangements would contemplate accommodations, signals, movement
                    into Berlin of necessary US troops and supplies simultaneously with our
                    withdrawal from Russian zone, and security measures. Deane is requested to
                    ascertain if Marshal Zhukov will designate representatives to discuss this
                    matter.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d66-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d66-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to the Acting Secretary of State over the signature of Jefferson Caffery,
                    American Ambassador to France.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d66-f2" n="2" xml:id="d66-f2-content">
                <p> Eisenhower’s telegram is not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
